root/root.rb:3: `Root` cannot be a `class`, because packages are nested under `Root` https://srb.help/4035
     3 |class Root < Prelude::A
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    root/__package.rb:3: Package `Root` defined here
     3 |class Root < PackageSpec
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    root/a/b/__package.rb:3: `Root::A::B` is nested under `Root`
     3 |class Root::A::B < PackageSpec
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  Note:
    Either make it a `module`, or move the packages nested under `Root` elsewhere.
    Defining behavior on a namespace that other packages are nested under is discouraged, because it slows down code loading in large codebases.
    If it's unavoidable, package `Root` can opt out of this restriction with `imported_by_nested_packages!`, which requires every package nested under `Root` to `import Root`
  Note:
    Until this is fixed, Sorbet isolates every definition of `Root` in this file, so the constants and methods they define don't resolve, even from inside them

